    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Brad Sherman has served in the U.S. House since 1997 and represents California's 32nd District. He is a senior member of the Foreign Affairs and Financial Services committees. He chaired the Subcommittee on Investor Protection and Capital Markets from 2019 to 2023. Before Congress, he chaired the California State Board of Equalization. He led the repeal of the state’s snack tax.",
        "cites": [1],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Brad Sherman has served in the U.S. House since 1997 and represents California's 32nd District.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He is a senior member of the Foreign Affairs and Financial Services committees.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He chaired the Subcommittee on Investor Protection and Capital Markets from 2019 to 2023.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "Before Congress, he chaired the California State Board of Equalization.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He led the repeal of the state’s snack tax.",
            "cites": [1]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In 2026, he introduced the Stop Oil Exports to Lower Gas Prices Act. Sherman joined a letter urging FEMA to release $745 million in hazard mitigation funds for Los Angeles wildfire recovery. According to his campaign, he has voted against funding ICE and authored the first articles of impeachment against President Trump. His campaign says he supports capping drug prices and advocates building a subway through the Sepulveda Pass.",
        "cites": [2, 3, 4],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "In 2026, he introduced the Stop Oil Exports to Lower Gas Prices Act.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "Sherman joined a letter urging FEMA to release $745 million in hazard mitigation funds for Los Angeles wildfire recovery.",
            "cites": [3]
          },
          {
            "text": "According to his campaign, he has voted against funding ICE and authored the first articles of impeachment against President Trump.",
            "cites": [4]
          },
          {
            "text": "His campaign says he supports capping drug prices and advocates building a subway through the Sepulveda Pass.",
            "cites": [4]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In 1997, he secured a $699 million appropriation for land acquisition. He also secured $20 million to complete the Backbone Trail. He helped create the Consumer Financial Protection Agency.",
        "cites": [1],
        "sentences": [
